hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3695","Dahhak bin Firoz Daylami narrates this statement of his father: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have accepted Islam, and I have two sisters in marriage, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Divorce one of them whomever you wish."
"3696","Dhahaq ibn Firoz Daylami narrates this statement of his father: When I accepted Islam, I had two sisters in marriage, the Prophet instructed me: I should divorce one of them."
"3697","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
